1
00:00:05,120 --> 00:00:06,680
Then I'm going to see my friends tonight.

2
00:00:06,960 --> 00:00:09,000
Can you please just do what I ask for once?

3
00:00:09,200 --> 00:00:10,000
Put, it hurts.

4
00:00:11,080 --> 00:00:11,880
Hey! Jane.

5
00:00:12,080 --> 00:00:12,600
Ow!

6
00:00:13,360 --> 00:00:14,320
How did you get here?

7
00:00:14,720 --> 00:00:15,240
Jane.

8
00:00:15,720 --> 00:00:16,800
I'm really sorry about just now.

9
00:00:19,000 --> 00:00:20,080
If you ever come near Jane again,

10
00:00:20,560 --> 00:00:21,920
I won't let you off easy.

11
00:00:22,240 --> 00:00:22,800
Hello, Jane?

12
00:00:23,200 --> 00:00:24,200
Get to the hospital right now.

13
00:00:24,360 --> 00:00:25,880
Put is in the ER room right now.

14
00:00:26,200 --> 00:00:27,240
P'Jane..

15
00:00:28,200 --> 00:00:29,680
Doctor.

16
00:00:29,920 --> 00:00:30,840
You killed Put, didn't you?

17
00:00:31,480 --> 00:00:33,000
Can you please trust me just this once?

18
00:00:33,480 --> 00:00:35,360
Ever since you came into my life,

19
00:00:35,600 --> 00:00:37,200
everything has been completely ruined.

20
00:00:37,560 --> 00:00:38,920
You're the person who gives anyone whatever

21
00:00:38,920 --> 00:00:40,080
they ask for, right?

22
00:00:40,240 --> 00:00:42,760
Then I'm asking you to disappear from my life.

23
00:00:43,280 --> 00:00:44,280
Then tonight,

24
00:00:44,880 --> 00:00:46,680
I ask to stay with you for one last night.

25
00:00:47,080 --> 00:00:48,120
And after this,

26
00:00:48,600 --> 00:00:50,280
I will disappear from your life.

27
00:00:50,680 --> 00:00:51,920
Love you with all my heart.

28
00:00:52,800 --> 00:00:53,920
Big Jane belongs to Little Jane.

29
00:01:29,400 --> 00:01:30,840
Jennalee?

30
00:01:32,280 --> 00:01:32,800
Yes.

31
00:01:33,000 --> 00:01:34,160
Please step into the interview room.

32
00:01:36,680 --> 00:01:37,320
This way, please.

33
00:01:48,320 --> 00:01:53,120
5 years later...

34
00:01:53,120 --> 00:01:54,920
Mr.Jennalee, what year did you graduate?

35
00:01:56,320 --> 00:01:58,000
In 2024.

36
00:01:59,000 --> 00:02:00,280
So it's been two years since you graduated.

37
00:02:01,440 --> 00:02:02,720
Looking at your work history,

38
00:02:03,080 --> 00:02:05,200
You used to work at a bank.

39
00:02:06,160 --> 00:02:07,440
Why did you decide to apply for

40
00:02:07,440 --> 00:02:09,400
an executive secretary position?

41
00:02:11,480 --> 00:02:12,720
I think I'm well-suited for work that

42
00:02:12,720 --> 00:02:14,200
requires attention to detail,

43
00:02:14,840 --> 00:02:16,560
and supporting others.

44
00:02:17,120 --> 00:02:18,880
If that's the case, you're aware of

45
00:02:18,880 --> 00:02:20,360
what our company does, right?

46
00:02:21,520 --> 00:02:22,200
Yes, I am.

47
00:02:23,200 --> 00:02:24,800
It's a venture capital firm

48
00:02:25,040 --> 00:02:26,880
that raises and manages funds

49
00:02:26,880 --> 00:02:28,880
to invest in startups with high potential

50
00:02:29,440 --> 00:02:31,240
for massive future growth.

51
00:02:31,560 --> 00:02:32,880
I also know

52
00:02:33,040 --> 00:02:35,880
that you are a very visionary co-founder,

53
00:02:36,400 --> 00:02:37,560
having invested in several startups

54
00:02:37,560 --> 00:02:38,960
that went on to become unicorns.

55
00:02:42,400 --> 00:02:42,920
To be honest,

56
00:02:42,920 --> 00:02:44,079
I've been following your work quite closely.

57
00:02:46,800 --> 00:02:47,960
Flattery will get you everywhere.

58
00:02:49,160 --> 00:02:51,120
Do you think compliments will get you the job?

59
00:02:53,880 --> 00:02:54,480
No, not at all.

60
00:02:55,480 --> 00:02:56,680
I really do follow your work.

61
00:02:58,040 --> 00:03:00,280
But you know that the position you're applying for

62
00:03:00,640 --> 00:03:01,720
isn't for my secretary, right?

63
00:03:03,440 --> 00:03:04,040
Yes, I know.

64
00:03:05,080 --> 00:03:06,520
It's for Ms.Lilac,

65
00:03:07,040 --> 00:03:08,120
the new CEO who

66
00:03:08,600 --> 00:03:10,120
just acquired a major stake last month.

67
00:03:10,960 --> 00:03:11,440
That's correct.

68
00:03:12,000 --> 00:03:14,120
When it comes to global track records,

69
00:03:14,640 --> 00:03:16,840
Lilac has far more experience than I do.

70
00:03:19,600 --> 00:03:20,079
Right.

71
00:03:28,600 --> 00:03:29,800
One last question..

72
00:03:31,680 --> 00:03:33,079
Jennalee,

73
00:03:34,079 --> 00:03:34,840
how do you envision yourself

74
00:03:34,840 --> 00:03:36,040
as an executive secretary?

75
00:03:48,280 --> 00:03:49,280
Everyone always says

76
00:03:50,520 --> 00:03:52,200
that I'm the type of person who will do anything

77
00:03:52,200 --> 00:03:53,200
if asked for help.

78
00:03:57,600 --> 00:03:59,160
So I think I would be a secretary

79
00:04:00,200 --> 00:04:01,840
who, no matter what my boss asks me to do,

80
00:04:03,880 --> 00:04:05,000
will always deliver.

81
00:04:10,160 --> 00:04:10,960
Really?

82
00:04:14,520 --> 00:04:16,880
Then I ask for you to belong to me alone.

83
00:04:36,920 --> 00:04:37,960
Jennalee?

84
00:04:39,720 --> 00:04:40,520
Jennalee?

85
00:04:44,600 --> 00:04:45,520
are you alright?

86
00:04:48,800 --> 00:04:49,560
No, it's nothing.

87
00:05:00,760 --> 00:05:02,600
Ah, please sit down first then.

88
00:05:10,640 --> 00:05:11,560
I would like to tell you that,

89
00:05:12,280 --> 00:05:13,720
for our company,

90
00:05:14,400 --> 00:05:15,880
before helping others,

91
00:05:16,920 --> 00:05:18,920
we must prioritize the company's

92
00:05:18,920 --> 00:05:20,000
best interests first.

93
00:05:24,280 --> 00:05:26,040
That will be all for today, Jennalee.

94
00:05:26,440 --> 00:05:28,120
We will notify you of the interview

95
00:05:28,120 --> 00:05:29,440
results by email.

96
00:05:30,480 --> 00:05:31,320
Good luck.

97
00:05:36,880 --> 00:05:37,440
Thank you.

98
00:06:01,400 --> 00:06:05,840
You walk in with a warning sign

99
00:06:08,200 --> 00:06:13,320
Just one look and already falling for you

100
00:06:15,760 --> 00:06:20,400
My friends tell me not to cross that line

101
00:06:22,720 --> 00:06:27,720
But I’m already out of time

102
00:06:29,680 --> 00:06:31,760
I know the truth, I taste the sin

103
00:06:31,760 --> 00:06:33,400
It’s wrong but I don’t want it to be true

104
00:06:33,400 --> 00:06:35,920
I’m losing all my discipline

105
00:06:36,120 --> 00:06:40,040
You’re all I’m thinking of

106
00:06:40,040 --> 00:06:42,120
and I’m breaking all the rules

107
00:06:42,120 --> 00:06:44,400
just because…

108
00:06:44,400 --> 00:06:47,800
You’re a red flag but I’m colorblind

109
00:06:47,800 --> 00:06:51,200
I know you’re dangerous

110
00:06:51,640 --> 00:06:55,040
If it burns, let it burn me alive

111
00:06:55,040 --> 00:06:59,320
I can't hold myself back, I’d cross every line

112
00:07:04,960 --> 00:07:07,600
Ooh

113
00:08:00,800 --> 00:08:02,480
How did the

114
00:08:04,600 --> 00:08:05,400
job interview go?

115
00:08:08,040 --> 00:08:08,520
Well...

116
00:08:09,120 --> 00:08:10,000
Nothing special.

117
00:08:11,520 --> 00:08:12,680
They just asked about...

118
00:08:12,840 --> 00:08:14,040
my previous work experience,

119
00:08:14,360 --> 00:08:15,640
and why I applied.

120
00:08:16,880 --> 00:08:18,600
Just standard stuff about the company.

121
00:08:19,200 --> 00:08:19,720
Mm.

122
00:08:21,960 --> 00:08:22,480
Mm.

123
00:08:24,240 --> 00:08:25,800
And when will you know the results?

124
00:08:27,280 --> 00:08:29,520
They said they'd let me know by email.

125
00:08:30,080 --> 00:08:30,600
Is that so?

126
00:08:30,840 --> 00:08:32,080
I don't know when either.

127
00:08:32,640 --> 00:08:33,159
Mm.

128
00:08:35,200 --> 00:08:36,159
Truth be told,

129
00:08:36,760 --> 00:08:37,440
I still feel that

130
00:08:38,159 --> 00:08:39,880
it's a shame about your old job.

131
00:08:40,679 --> 00:08:42,440
Banking is stable,

132
00:08:42,679 --> 00:08:43,600
and the pay is good.

133
00:08:44,200 --> 00:08:46,520
Why couldn't you have stuck it out a little longer?

134
00:08:46,520 --> 00:08:47,640
Why were you in such a rush to resign?

135
00:08:48,240 --> 00:08:49,000
Oh, come on.

136
00:08:49,120 --> 00:08:50,400
Bank jobs nowadays

137
00:08:50,400 --> 00:08:51,840
aren't like they used to be.

138
00:08:51,840 --> 00:08:53,600
They aren't that stable anymore.

139
00:08:54,200 --> 00:08:55,240
Did you see the news?

140
00:08:55,560 --> 00:08:56,120
Just recently,

141
00:08:56,120 --> 00:08:58,000
they laid off entire teams of employees

142
00:08:58,320 --> 00:08:59,640
because everyone has switched to

143
00:08:59,640 --> 00:09:00,440
using mobile apps now.

144
00:09:01,440 --> 00:09:02,240
Uh...

145
00:09:04,840 --> 00:09:05,320
Hey.

146
00:09:05,800 --> 00:09:06,640
Not like Jet.

147
00:09:07,240 --> 00:09:09,400
He's studying Traditional Chinese Medicine.

148
00:09:09,400 --> 00:09:10,200
Once he graduates,

149
00:09:10,200 --> 00:09:11,800
he can come right back and work at the shop.

150
00:09:12,320 --> 00:09:13,440
I don't have to worry at all.

151
00:09:21,240 --> 00:09:22,040
Ah,

152
00:09:23,080 --> 00:09:24,440
let's eat.

153
00:09:25,880 --> 00:09:26,400
Ah...

154
00:09:32,800 --> 00:09:34,000
It's been five years since

155
00:09:34,520 --> 00:09:37,280
I parted ways with P'Jane back then.

156
00:09:39,200 --> 00:09:41,800
So many things have changed over time.

157
00:09:43,760 --> 00:09:45,160
Yet so many things

158
00:09:46,120 --> 00:09:47,680
haven't really changed much at all.

159
00:09:48,720 --> 00:09:49,200
Sis,

160
00:09:49,680 --> 00:09:51,160
give me a packet of herbal tea.

161
00:09:51,760 --> 00:09:52,560
Sure.

162
00:09:53,320 --> 00:09:54,800
My parents still run

163
00:09:54,800 --> 00:09:56,680
the Chinese herbal medicine shop just like before.

164
00:09:57,440 --> 00:09:59,360
Except now that they've gotten older,

165
00:09:59,360 --> 00:10:00,120
Oh!

166
00:10:00,520 --> 00:10:02,280
They can't do heavy work like they used to. Oh dear!

167
00:10:02,280 --> 00:10:02,880
Mom!

168
00:10:03,640 --> 00:10:04,920
Why didn't you tell me if you needed something?

169
00:10:05,280 --> 00:10:05,960
Ouch...

170
00:10:05,960 --> 00:10:08,080
I was just reaching to get the herbal tea for the auntie.

171
00:10:08,760 --> 00:10:09,280
It hurts.

172
00:10:10,120 --> 00:10:10,800
Go, go, go.

173
00:10:10,800 --> 00:10:11,880
Mom, go sit down first.

174
00:10:11,880 --> 00:10:12,680
Yeah, yeah.

175
00:10:12,680 --> 00:10:13,280
Go get the medicine for the auntie first.

176
00:10:13,280 --> 00:10:14,160
The bitter herbal tea.

177
00:10:23,480 --> 00:10:24,800
Jet enrolled in university

178
00:10:24,800 --> 00:10:26,040
in the Traditional Chinese Medicine faculty

179
00:10:26,040 --> 00:10:26,920
as mom wished,

180
00:10:27,200 --> 00:10:29,760
so he could graduate and help dad at the pharmacy.

181
00:10:30,400 --> 00:10:31,480
But he still hasn't given up on his dream

182
00:10:31,480 --> 00:10:32,880
of becoming an idol,

183
00:10:33,440 --> 00:10:34,960
frequently going to auditions...

184
00:10:35,960 --> 00:10:37,040
though he's never passed one.

185
00:10:37,600 --> 00:10:39,680
This texture is so light and airy!

186
00:10:39,800 --> 00:10:41,320
It's a total must-have, guys!

187
00:10:41,600 --> 00:10:43,840
This item is super cheap, guys!

188
00:10:43,960 --> 00:10:45,640
It's only two hundred baht!

189
00:10:46,680 --> 00:10:47,200
Bro!

190
00:10:47,240 --> 00:10:48,200
Come here quick!

191
00:10:49,800 --> 00:10:50,800
As for Jean,

192
00:10:51,520 --> 00:10:52,120
she just passed the entrance exam for

193
00:10:52,120 --> 00:10:53,040
Mass Communication,

194
00:10:53,760 --> 00:10:54,800
and is currently waiting for

195
00:10:54,800 --> 00:10:55,960
her first semester to start.

196
00:10:56,560 --> 00:10:57,320
Lately,

197
00:10:57,320 --> 00:10:58,560
she's been earning pocket money

198
00:10:58,560 --> 00:11:00,080
as a TikTok Live influencer.

199
00:11:15,080 --> 00:11:17,720
(Not posting work anymore? I'm waiting!)

200
00:11:17,720 --> 00:11:19,640
I stopped posting comic strips on Instagram.

201
00:11:20,880 --> 00:11:23,480
Even though drawing comics was my dream,

202
00:11:24,400 --> 00:11:25,480
now...

203
00:11:25,960 --> 00:11:27,600
I have to accept reality

204
00:11:28,280 --> 00:11:30,960
that I probably can't turn it into a career.

205
00:11:31,680 --> 00:11:32,760
I have Dad.

206
00:11:33,200 --> 00:11:33,880
Mom.

207
00:11:34,600 --> 00:11:37,040
And my younger siblings to take care of.

208
00:11:37,680 --> 00:11:39,360
I want everyone to be happy.

209
00:11:40,320 --> 00:11:41,040
Once I graduated,

210
00:11:41,960 --> 00:11:43,880
I started working at a bank.

211
00:11:45,000 --> 00:11:46,200
But the workload was huge,

212
00:11:46,960 --> 00:11:48,440
leaving me with barely any time to rest.

213
00:11:49,360 --> 00:11:50,400
I was super stressed,

214
00:11:51,000 --> 00:11:53,400
having to do unpaid overtime every single day,

215
00:11:53,680 --> 00:11:54,760
even though some of the work

216
00:11:55,280 --> 00:11:57,080
wasn't even my responsibility in the first place.

217
00:12:00,880 --> 00:12:02,440
(Gap)

218
00:12:02,440 --> 00:12:03,320
Until eventually,

219
00:12:04,280 --> 00:12:05,880
Gap recommended that I apply to work

220
00:12:05,880 --> 00:12:06,560
at the same company as him

221
00:12:07,720 --> 00:12:08,680
which is

222
00:12:09,240 --> 00:12:11,440
the very company I just interviewed with.

223
00:12:12,040 --> 00:12:12,960
Hello, Gap.

224
00:12:13,120 --> 00:12:13,600
Hello?

225
00:12:13,840 --> 00:12:14,320
Uh...

226
00:12:14,480 --> 00:12:15,120
How'd it go?

227
00:12:15,120 --> 00:12:16,040
The interview today?

228
00:12:16,920 --> 00:12:17,680
I don't know, man.

229
00:12:18,920 --> 00:12:20,040
I'm not sure if I'll get it.

230
00:12:20,680 --> 00:12:22,880
Ms.Rin is super intimidating.

231
00:12:24,760 --> 00:12:25,960
She has such a poker face.

232
00:12:26,280 --> 00:12:27,760
I don't know if she likes me or not.

233
00:12:29,880 --> 00:12:32,400
So when I first walked in, right?

234
00:12:33,160 --> 00:12:34,120
She...

235
00:12:35,120 --> 00:12:36,760
She didn't even greet me or anything.

236
00:12:36,760 --> 00:12:38,360
It's like...

237
00:13:26,400 --> 00:13:28,040
As for P'Jane,

238
00:13:29,960 --> 00:13:31,280
by now, I know

239
00:13:32,480 --> 00:13:35,120
that P'Jane had nothing to do with Put's death.

240
00:13:37,640 --> 00:13:39,480
The real culprit was caught.

241
00:13:49,880 --> 00:13:51,440
As for this condo,

242
00:13:52,000 --> 00:13:53,880
P'Jane left the keycard for me,

243
00:13:55,200 --> 00:13:56,600
along with a note saying

244
00:13:57,160 --> 00:13:58,680
I could come whenever I wanted.

245
00:14:00,360 --> 00:14:02,160
I come here periodically,

246
00:14:03,120 --> 00:14:05,200
just in case P'Jane might come back here sometime.

247
00:14:12,080 --> 00:14:14,160
I feel really guilty

248
00:14:15,160 --> 00:14:17,200
that I told him to get out of my life.

249
00:14:26,640 --> 00:14:27,880
After that day

250
00:14:28,920 --> 00:14:30,040
five years ago,

251
00:14:32,840 --> 00:14:35,200
P'Jane really disappeared from my life.

252
00:14:38,800 --> 00:14:41,080
I tried searching for P'Jane everywhere

253
00:14:44,240 --> 00:14:45,400
that we used to be together,

254
00:15:17,000 --> 00:15:18,280
but I never found him.

255
00:15:20,800 --> 00:15:22,200
I always wondered

256
00:15:23,560 --> 00:15:24,880
where P'Jane went.

257
00:15:33,240 --> 00:15:35,200
I might not be able to say with full confidence

258
00:15:35,880 --> 00:15:37,560
that P'Jane is a good person,

259
00:15:40,120 --> 00:15:41,760
but I loved him so much,

260
00:15:43,080 --> 00:15:46,080
and I still love him to this day.

261
00:15:52,400 --> 00:15:54,760
I hope P'Jane hasn't forgotten me either.

262
00:16:11,160 --> 00:16:13,760
When you said you loved me,

263
00:16:14,160 --> 00:16:17,840
or were you just saying it?

264
00:16:17,840 --> 00:16:21,200
Because what you did makes it so clear

265
00:16:21,640 --> 00:16:23,120
You tricked me into loving you,

266
00:16:23,360 --> 00:16:26,800
and then you destroyed me

267
00:16:27,120 --> 00:16:28,960
You said you loved me,

268
00:16:29,480 --> 00:16:33,120
yet you hurt me

269
00:16:33,320 --> 00:16:36,560
The more I love you,

270
00:16:36,840 --> 00:16:38,680
the more it hurts

271
00:16:38,960 --> 00:16:41,240
I just want to know,

272
00:16:41,240 --> 00:16:43,200
did you ever love me?

273
00:16:43,960 --> 00:16:44,960
But then

274
00:16:45,800 --> 00:16:46,760
reality pulled it's grip on me back

275
00:16:46,760 --> 00:16:48,800
into the real world again.

276
00:16:56,760 --> 00:16:58,360
Ugh,

277
00:16:58,360 --> 00:17:00,240
when the hell are you going to open it, huh?

278
00:17:00,400 --> 00:17:01,040
What are you waiting for?

279
00:17:01,560 --> 00:17:03,480
Give him some time to brace himself!

280
00:17:03,480 --> 00:17:04,359
Why are you rushing him?

281
00:17:04,520 --> 00:17:06,040
Yeah! And why are you arguing with me,

282
00:17:06,040 --> 00:17:06,520
huh?

283
00:17:06,680 --> 00:17:07,800
Because I want to know!

284
00:17:08,119 --> 00:17:09,280
Enough, you two.

285
00:17:09,280 --> 00:17:10,160
Bickering ever since student days

286
00:17:10,160 --> 00:17:10,760
all the way into working life.

287
00:17:10,760 --> 00:17:11,560
Just bickering non-stop.

288
00:17:11,800 --> 00:17:13,000
Yeah, because of you!

289
