Could you turn around for a moment?

582
00:34:00,000 --> 00:34:01,200
These are all the documents

583
00:34:01,200 --> 00:34:02,200
that need your signature today.

584
00:34:13,120 --> 00:34:13,800
Understood.

585
00:34:21,639 --> 00:34:22,159
It's just...

586
00:34:22,600 --> 00:34:23,080
P'Jane...

587
00:34:23,080 --> 00:34:24,159
Give me some time to read them.

588
00:34:25,600 --> 00:34:26,719
If anything comes up, I'll call you.

589
00:34:36,360 --> 00:34:37,000
Got it.

590
00:35:07,920 --> 00:35:09,400
Jane,

591
00:35:09,400 --> 00:35:10,440
could you do me a favor

592
00:35:10,440 --> 00:35:13,440
and draft the meeting summary report for me?

593
00:35:25,200 --> 00:35:28,200
But isn't this report under your responsibility?

594
00:35:30,200 --> 00:35:31,280
Well, yes...

595
00:35:31,280 --> 00:35:32,440
Jane,

596
00:35:32,440 --> 00:35:34,200
our hands are already full with work.

597
00:35:34,200 --> 00:35:35,120
Could you give us a hand?

598
00:35:35,480 --> 00:35:36,760
Besides, this report

599
00:35:36,760 --> 00:35:38,520
is also meant for Mr.Lilac, you know.

600
00:35:41,880 --> 00:35:43,560
I'm sorry, P'Big, P'Sue,

601
00:35:44,680 --> 00:35:45,480
but I also have work

602
00:35:45,480 --> 00:35:46,560
that I need to complete for Mr.Lilac.

603
00:35:53,120 --> 00:35:54,080
It's fine...

604
00:35:54,080 --> 00:35:54,640
I'll just...

605
00:35:55,400 --> 00:35:56,120
Oh! Oh dear!

606
00:35:57,400 --> 00:35:58,680
What's wrong, Sis?

607
00:35:59,680 --> 00:36:02,960
I'm just feeling a bit unwell.

608
00:36:03,160 --> 00:36:05,600
I went to the hospital yesterday

609
00:36:06,000 --> 00:36:07,000
and haven't slept at all.

610
00:36:07,480 --> 00:36:08,800
Oh my god, if you're this sick,

611
00:36:08,800 --> 00:36:10,240
should you take leave and see a doctor?

612
00:36:11,280 --> 00:36:11,880
I can't.

613
00:36:11,880 --> 00:36:12,680
Can you handle this?

614
00:36:12,920 --> 00:36:15,800
I have to finish this report,

615
00:36:15,800 --> 00:36:17,600
because I need to submit it to Mr.Lilac later.

616
00:36:17,600 --> 00:36:19,320
It's fine, I'll go do it myself.

617
00:36:21,720 --> 00:36:23,120
If she doesn't finish it,

618
00:36:23,440 --> 00:36:25,400
Mr.Lilac's work will be stalled as well, Jane.

619
00:36:25,400 --> 00:36:26,400
Please help us out.

620
00:36:27,920 --> 00:36:28,920
Are you okay?

621
00:36:30,440 --> 00:36:31,600
Come on. Are you okay, Sis?

622
00:36:33,960 --> 00:36:34,600
Alright then.

623
00:36:39,880 --> 00:36:40,680
If that's the case,

624
00:36:41,360 --> 00:36:42,760
I'll leave it in your hands.

625
00:36:44,280 --> 00:36:45,080
Are you okay?

626
00:36:45,560 --> 00:36:46,680
Come on, let's go see a doctor.

627
00:37:01,200 --> 00:37:01,760
Why the hell did you meddle

628
00:37:01,760 --> 00:37:03,480
and take on her work?

629
00:37:04,040 --> 00:37:04,520
You know damn well

630
00:37:04,520 --> 00:37:06,880
she was lying just to use you!

631
00:37:07,320 --> 00:37:08,080
Yeah,

632
00:37:09,080 --> 00:37:10,000
I know.

633
00:37:11,760 --> 00:37:12,880
I just didn't want any drama.

634
00:37:15,080 --> 00:37:17,280
Dammit, you're always like this!

635
00:37:18,120 --> 00:37:19,240
Come on,

636
00:37:20,360 --> 00:37:21,400
once this project is done,

637
00:37:21,400 --> 00:37:22,400
I'll go clear things with her myself.

638
00:37:23,280 --> 00:37:24,360
I want to talk nicely to her first.

639
00:37:26,000 --> 00:37:27,080
But if reasoning with her doesn't work,

640
00:37:27,240 --> 00:37:28,600
you better tell P'Jane right away, man.

641
00:37:39,680 --> 00:37:41,280
And how are things with P'Jane anyway?

642
00:37:44,200 --> 00:37:45,200
Is everything okay?

643
00:37:48,560 --> 00:37:49,880
I feel so extremely uncomfortable.

644
00:37:53,000 --> 00:37:53,760
I've been working with him

645
00:37:53,760 --> 00:37:54,640
for two weeks now,

646
00:37:56,000 --> 00:37:57,840
and he keeps acting so distant with me all the time.

647
00:38:01,200 --> 00:38:02,400
I really want to apologize to him.

648
00:38:05,600 --> 00:38:06,520
Bro...

649
00:38:07,080 --> 00:38:08,080
Why don't you try asking

650
00:38:08,080 --> 00:38:10,080
to clear things out directly with him?

651
00:38:11,360 --> 00:38:12,800
Every time I bring it up,

652
00:38:13,080 --> 00:38:14,280
he always cuts me off.

653
00:38:15,680 --> 00:38:16,800
I think

654
00:38:17,680 --> 00:38:19,240
he must still be mad at me.

655
00:38:23,400 --> 00:38:25,040
I refused to trust him,

656
00:38:29,000 --> 00:38:30,200
and on top of that, I drove him away.

657
00:38:34,720 --> 00:38:35,920
Hey, hey,

658
00:38:36,080 --> 00:38:37,280
take it easy, man.

659
00:38:49,320 --> 00:38:50,120
Things will get better.

660
00:38:53,880 --> 00:38:54,800
Didn't even wait to toast with me...

661
00:39:39,760 --> 00:39:40,640
P'Nut,

662
00:39:41,000 --> 00:39:42,000
could you please open

663
00:39:42,000 --> 00:39:44,080
the price quote for Ms.Nanthana?

664
00:40:00,560 --> 00:40:02,920
I think the numbers right here don't match up.

665
00:40:04,200 --> 00:40:05,680
Could you please edit this for me again?

666
00:40:05,680 --> 00:40:06,560
Please double check it one more time.

667
00:40:07,440 --> 00:40:07,960
Thank you!

668
00:40:16,480 --> 00:40:17,200
Excuse me,

669
00:40:17,680 --> 00:40:18,480
uh...

670
00:40:19,280 --> 00:40:21,600
This is actually the old contract.

671
00:40:32,120 --> 00:40:33,280
P'...

672
00:40:33,480 --> 00:40:34,440
Steph. Yes?

673
00:40:34,680 --> 00:40:36,000
Right, P'Steph.

674
00:40:37,080 --> 00:40:37,880
Uh...

675
00:40:39,160 --> 00:40:40,480
I think this one is...

676
00:40:40,880 --> 00:40:41,800
the old deal.

677
00:40:48,920 --> 00:40:50,000
It's all done, P'Sue.

678
00:40:50,680 --> 00:40:52,640
Got it, I'll take a look for you.

679
00:40:55,480 --> 00:40:58,360
The numbers on these two pages look weird.

680
00:40:58,480 --> 00:41:00,320
Could you double-check them again for me?

681
00:41:00,320 --> 00:41:02,280
I think these might be wrong, and...

682
00:41:02,520 --> 00:41:04,480
here as well.

683
00:41:04,680 --> 00:41:09,080
Could you try reworking it and show it to me again?

684
00:41:09,400 --> 00:41:11,040
Just a tiny bit,

685
00:41:11,600 --> 00:41:12,800
just a little bit.

686
00:41:12,800 --> 00:41:16,200
It's just editing a page or two, and then

687
00:41:16,200 --> 00:41:17,160
print it out and then

688
00:41:17,160 --> 00:41:20,000
I'll have her approve it right away,

689
00:41:20,000 --> 00:41:20,800
okay?

690
00:41:21,120 --> 00:41:23,000
It should be doable by 3:00 PM, right?

691
00:41:23,000 --> 00:41:24,440
This should take...

692
00:41:24,840 --> 00:41:26,560
oh, just a moment!

693
00:41:26,560 --> 00:41:28,240
A few keystrokes and it's done.

694
00:41:28,240 --> 00:41:29,920
I'll leave it to you!

695
00:41:29,920 --> 00:41:31,080
Alright, okay!

696
00:41:32,200 --> 00:41:35,600
And she, like, totally loves it!

697
00:41:35,600 --> 00:41:36,760
P'Tao is so fabulous!

698
00:41:36,760 --> 00:41:37,480
Yeah!

699
00:41:37,480 --> 00:41:38,880
Just go on holiday!

700
00:41:45,040 --> 00:41:45,880
Oh my!

701
00:41:57,200 --> 00:41:58,120
Jennalee.

702
00:42:03,400 --> 00:42:04,000
Yes?

703
00:42:07,360 --> 00:42:09,000
Please see me in my office.

704
00:42:14,640 --> 00:42:15,280
Right away.

705
00:42:23,760 --> 00:42:25,000
He's definitely getting called in

706
00:42:25,000 --> 00:42:26,480
to get chewed out by Mr.Lilac.

707
00:42:26,480 --> 00:42:29,320
For sure, a hundred percent.

708
00:42:29,600 --> 00:42:30,400
Oops!

709
00:42:31,200 --> 00:42:32,200
Hang in there!

710
00:42:32,200 --> 00:42:33,000
Hang in there!

711
00:42:35,400 --> 00:42:36,520
I'm rooting for you!

712
00:42:37,960 --> 00:42:38,480
He's definitely getting it.

713
00:42:39,600 --> 00:42:40,280
So satisfying.

714
00:42:48,360 --> 00:42:49,560
What have you been up to lately, Jane?

715
00:42:53,120 --> 00:42:53,640
Well...

716
00:42:54,400 --> 00:42:55,280
Just working.

717
00:43:03,560 --> 00:43:04,440
I know.

718
00:43:05,760 --> 00:43:06,720
What I mean is...

719
00:43:07,160 --> 00:43:09,000
why do you seem so busy all the time lately?

720
00:43:09,960 --> 00:43:10,880
Working late into the night.

721
00:43:11,320 --> 00:43:12,520
Did I give you too much work?

722
00:43:21,960 --> 00:43:23,320
I've read the weekly reports

723
00:43:23,320 --> 00:43:24,760
from the other executives.

724
00:43:28,880 --> 00:43:30,000
You wrote them, didn't you?

725
00:43:36,000 --> 00:43:36,680
You know that?

726
00:43:36,680 --> 00:43:37,520
Why wouldn't I know?

727
00:43:38,720 --> 00:43:40,280
How many times have we written reports together?

728
00:43:41,320 --> 00:43:43,560
I recognize your writing style.

729
00:43:48,920 --> 00:43:50,400
Could you please wait until this project is finished?

730
00:43:51,560 --> 00:43:53,320
I'll go talk to P'Big and P'Sue myself.

731
00:43:55,880 --> 00:43:57,160
And don't worry, P'Jane,

732
00:43:57,400 --> 00:43:59,040
that I won't finish your work.

733
00:44:11,720 --> 00:44:12,240
Sue,

734
00:44:12,600 --> 00:44:13,120
Big,

735
00:44:14,520 --> 00:44:15,200
please step inside for a moment.

736
00:44:32,480 --> 00:44:33,800
Didn't I tell you before?

737
00:44:35,600 --> 00:44:37,680
Don't be too emotional.

738
00:44:46,480 --> 00:44:47,600
Excuse me.

739
00:44:49,240 --> 00:44:49,880
How was it?

740
00:44:50,280 --> 00:44:50,880
What's the vibe?

741
00:44:50,880 --> 00:44:51,760
What's the vibe? Are you okay?

742
00:44:52,360 --> 00:44:53,120
Can you handle it?

743
00:45:04,400 --> 00:45:06,680
I've read your weekly reports.

744
00:45:09,440 --> 00:45:10,520
They are very well written.

745
00:45:12,520 --> 00:45:13,320
Thank you.

746
00:45:13,520 --> 00:45:14,880
Thank you, Mr.Lilac.

747
00:45:19,880 --> 00:45:21,040
However, I know

748
00:45:22,680 --> 00:45:24,800
that my secretary wrote this report.

749
00:45:31,800 --> 00:45:33,480
Jennalee didn't tell on you.

750
00:45:36,000 --> 00:45:36,880
In fact,

751
00:45:37,560 --> 00:45:38,840
if I hadn't caught on,

752
00:45:40,080 --> 00:45:41,400
he wouldn't have told me at all.

753
00:45:48,280 --> 00:45:49,120
Oh.

754
00:45:50,800 --> 00:45:52,520
And don't think I don't know

755
00:45:53,800 --> 00:45:55,240
what you two

756
00:45:56,080 --> 00:45:57,400
lied to me about.

757
00:46:04,920 --> 00:46:07,440
Let me reiterate Jennalee's position once again:

758
00:46:11,400 --> 00:46:12,600
Jennalee

759
00:46:13,720 --> 00:46:15,360
is my personal secretary

760
00:46:17,440 --> 00:46:18,560
and mine only.

761
00:46:22,040 --> 00:46:23,880
If anyone gives him other work to do again,

762
00:46:25,120 --> 00:46:26,360
it's equivalent to messing with my person

763
00:46:26,360 --> 00:46:27,480
without permission.

764
00:46:32,840 --> 00:46:34,280
That's all I have to say.

765
00:46:36,480 --> 00:46:38,400
I hope you understand what I mean.

766
00:46:39,400 --> 00:46:40,440
Yes, I understand.

767
00:46:40,680 --> 00:46:41,320
I understand.

768
00:46:41,440 --> 00:46:42,240
We're sorry.

769
00:46:42,880 --> 00:46:43,760
We're sorry.

770
00:47:22,040 --> 00:47:22,640
Thank you.

771
00:47:36,240 --> 00:47:37,480
Thank you, P'Jane,

772
00:47:38,880 --> 00:47:40,240
for always helping me.

773
00:47:42,840 --> 00:47:44,400
Well, you're my secretary.

774
00:48:37,760 --> 00:48:40,120
(Jennalee Tanapatpibul)

775
00:48:40,120 --> 00:48:42,720
(Personal Executive Assistant)

776
00:48:45,840 --> 00:48:47,400
Argh.

777
00:48:50,360 --> 00:48:51,040
Jane!

778
00:48:53,440 --> 00:48:53,960
Oh,

779
00:48:54,000 --> 00:48:54,720
P'Dan!

780
00:48:56,600 --> 00:48:57,680
How come you're here?

781
00:48:58,520 --> 00:49:00,040
I came to pitch for funding

782
00:49:00,400 --> 00:49:01,720
for the app I'm working on with my friends.

783
00:49:02,600 --> 00:49:04,080
Your app is being pitched today too?

784
00:49:04,280 --> 00:49:04,800
Yeah,

785
00:49:05,240 --> 00:49:06,200
the MyFarm app.

786
00:49:06,640 --> 00:49:07,360
Hey,

787
00:49:08,280 --> 00:49:09,080
I read about it.

788
00:49:09,560 --> 00:49:10,400
It's really interesting!

789
00:49:11,120 --> 00:49:11,920
Thanks!

790
00:49:14,440 --> 00:49:14,920
So...

791
00:49:14,920 --> 00:49:15,920
do you work here, Jane?

792
00:49:17,960 --> 00:49:18,440
Yeah,

793
00:49:19,240 --> 00:49:21,040
I'm the CEO's secretary.

794
00:49:32,840 --> 00:49:33,360
Jane,

795
00:49:34,760 --> 00:49:35,680
it's time for the pitch.

796
00:49:35,800 --> 00:49:36,880
Mr.Lilac is waiting.

797
00:49:37,480 --> 00:49:37,960
Oh,

798
00:49:38,280 --> 00:49:39,600
Dan is right here too.

799
00:49:40,200 --> 00:49:41,200
Please, come on in.

800
00:49:41,680 --> 00:49:42,160
Sure.

801
00:49:42,800 --> 00:49:43,480
After you.

802
00:50:03,000 --> 00:50:03,480
Dan?

803
00:50:04,280 --> 00:50:04,800
Dan?

804
00:50:05,000 --> 00:50:05,520
Please go ahead.

805
00:51:06,000 --> 00:51:07,400
I'm giving you three minutes.

806
00:51:09,400 --> 00:51:10,800
Pitch your project.

807
00:51:29,000 --> 00:51:29,880
Hello, everyone.

808
00:51:31,400 --> 00:51:33,680
The application I'm seeking funding for today

809
00:51:34,080 --> 00:51:34,720
is

810
00:51:35,400 --> 00:51:36,360
MyFarm.

811
00:51:37,040 --> 00:51:38,920
It's a marketplace application

812
00:51:38,920 --> 00:51:40,800
for premium-grade agricultural products

813
00:51:41,120 --> 00:51:43,360
that makes it convenient for farmers

814
00:51:43,360 --> 00:51:46,280
to present their produce directly to customers.

815
00:51:49,600 --> 00:51:51,520
The main problem we identified

816
00:51:51,520 --> 00:51:53,040
that led us to invent this app

817
00:51:53,280 --> 00:51:58,480
is selling through middlemen

818
00:51:58,960 --> 00:52:00,000
prices get squeezed,

819
00:52:00,280 --> 00:52:03,080
it's hard to reach premium customers,

820
00:52:03,520 --> 00:52:05,120
origin is unknown,

821
00:52:05,320 --> 00:52:06,640
quality is inconsistent,

822
00:52:06,640 --> 00:52:07,960
produce isn't actually fresh,

823
00:52:08,280 --> 00:52:11,360
and there's no traceability system.

824
00:52:11,480 --> 00:52:12,920
As for our target audience,

825
00:52:13,200 --> 00:52:16,440
they are between 25 to 45 years old,

826
00:52:16,560 --> 00:52:19,200
health-conscious, love organic products,

827
00:52:20,080 --> 00:52:21,920
and quality farms

828
00:52:21,920 --> 00:52:24,320
that want to sell directly using technology.

829
00:52:24,800 --> 00:52:28,680
Our marketing strategy is divided into two parts:

830
00:52:28,880 --> 00:52:31,280
online and on-site.

831
00:52:33,840 --> 00:52:35,440
Going back a moment ago,

832
00:52:36,200 --> 00:52:38,960
this is the basic look of our application.

833
00:52:38,960 --> 00:52:40,520
You can take a look.

834
00:52:42,320 --> 00:52:43,480
In conclusion,

835
00:52:43,800 --> 00:52:45,800
that wraps up my presentation.

836
00:52:53,280 --> 00:52:54,040
Hey,

837
00:52:54,040 --> 00:52:56,360
a guy who loves nature is so cool, right?

838
00:52:56,680 --> 00:52:57,480
Yeah,

839
00:52:57,600 --> 00:52:59,800
this eco-friendly project is really interesting!

840
00:53:08,120 --> 00:53:08,920
Next up

841
00:53:09,280 --> 00:53:10,400
is the Q&A session.

842
00:53:11,080 --> 00:53:13,160
Does anyone have any questions?

843
00:53:20,520 --> 00:53:22,200
How much funding are you asking for,

844
00:53:23,440 --> 00:53:25,040
and what percentage of the company are you offering?

845
00:53:28,480 --> 00:53:29,440
Ten million baht

846
00:53:30,320 --> 00:53:31,480
for twenty-five percent.

847
00:53:33,520 --> 00:53:35,640
Do you really think your company's valuation

848
00:53:38,480 --> 00:53:39,800
is forty million?

849
00:53:44,840 --> 00:53:45,320
Yes.

850
00:53:46,600 --> 00:53:48,480
I am confident in our potential.

851
00:54:02,000 --> 00:54:03,800
We'll review the details

852
00:54:03,800 --> 00:54:05,160
and consider it first.

853
00:54:05,760 --> 00:54:07,200
If there are any updates,

854
00:54:07,200 --> 00:54:09,080
I will reach out to you.

855
00:54:10,400 --> 00:54:10,920
Understood.

856
00:54:11,440 --> 00:54:12,240
Thank you.

857
00:54:57,400 --> 00:54:58,000
Dan.

858
00:55:07,040 --> 00:55:07,880
How are you getting home, Jane?

859
00:55:09,720 --> 00:55:10,800
I was about to call a ride.

860
00:55:11,360 --> 00:55:12,920
Jet took the car today.

861
00:55:13,680 --> 00:55:14,280
Hmm.

862
00:55:14,640 --> 00:55:15,200
In that case,

863
00:55:16,160 --> 00:55:17,240
let me give you a ride home.

864
00:55:18,040 --> 00:55:19,200
I remember the way to your house.

865
00:55:20,040 --> 00:55:20,680
It's alright.

866
00:55:24,560 --> 00:55:25,240
Come on.

867
00:55:25,640 --> 00:55:26,680
No need to overthink it.

868
00:55:27,840 --> 00:55:29,640
Besides, I want to visit

869
00:55:30,040 --> 00:55:31,480
your parents, Jane.

870
00:55:42,640 --> 00:55:43,280
Come here.

871
00:55:51,560 --> 00:55:52,360
